            <ArticleTitle>The costoclavicular syndrome: a 'new cause'.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>916-20</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Costoclavicular compression in obese, heavy breasted, middle aged or elderly women from tight, narrow brassiere straps is a common cause of neck, shoulder, and arm pain. Clues to diagnosis and simple treatment measures, including the use of a shoulder pad, are described.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
